 "summary": "Switches the mining block template manager's WaitAndCreateNewBlock loop from NodeClock to SteadyClock for timeout and fee polling tick measurements. NodeClock is retained strictly for checking the testnet 20-minute minimum difficulty rule against tip timestamps, and header documentation is added explaining the 20-minute difficulty constraint.",
 "problem": "WaitAndCreateNewBlock previously measured its overall timeout and 1-second fee polling interval using the wall clock (NodeClock). System wall clock adjustments could artificially lengthen or shorten wait durations, and frozen mocktime during testing prevented the wait from ever timing out.",
 "evidence": [
  "Commit 15186686ac: 'waitNext measures its timeout and 1-second fee tick with the wall clock, while waitTipChanged uses the steady clock. This means a wall clock jump changes how long waitNext waits, and it never times out while mocktime is frozen.'"
